=== QT024 | sorted attribute on a literal out of order
r:`s#3 1 2

=== QT024 | symbols sort by byte, so a lowercase before an uppercase is out of order
r:`s#`a`B

=== QT024 | unique attribute on a repeated item
r:`u#1 1 2

=== QT024 | parted attribute on a value that comes back
r:`p#1 2 1

=== clean | ties, a null first and contiguous runs are what the attributes allow
r1:`s#1 1 2
r2:`s#0N 1 2
r3:`p#1 1 2
r4:`s#`B`a

=== clean | grouped never fails, and a literal that runs on is not the operand
r1:`g#1 2 1
r2:`s#3 1 2,0

=== QE006 | a date that does not exist
r:2024.02.30

=== QE006 | 1900 was not a leap year
r:1900.02.29

=== QE006 | nor is there a thirteenth month
r:2024.13m

=== clean | 2000 was, and a path or a string with a bad date in it is not a literal
r1:2000.02.29
p:`:hdb/2024.02.30
s:"2024.02.30"

=== QE007 | select with no from
r:select a by b t

=== QE007 | inside a lambda too
f:{select x}

=== clean | a from anywhere before the statement ends, or the name assigned
r1:select from t
r2:update a:1 from t
.my.select:1

=== QT025 | signalling a number
f:{'1}

=== QT025 | a one-character string is a char atom, not a string
f:{'"x"}

=== clean | a string and a symbol
f1:{'"xy"}
f2:{'`a}

=== QE009 | while x'1 is each applied by juxtaposition (q 5: parse "{x'1}" is ')
f3:{x'1}

=== QT026 | lj with an unkeyed table on the right
t:([]a:1 2;b:3 4)
r:t lj ([]a:1 2;c:3 4)

=== QT026 | a name holding one is no different
t:([]a:1 2;b:3 4)
u:([]a:1 2;c:3 4)
r:t ij u

=== clean | a keyed right table is what lj wants, and uj takes either
t:([]a:1 2;b:3 4)
r1:t lj ([a:1 2]c:3 4)
r2:t uj ([]a:1 2;c:3 4)

=== QT027 | one value per column
t:([]a:1 2;b:3 4)
`t insert (5;6;7)

=== clean | the right number of values
t:([]a:1 2;b:3 4)
`t insert (5;6)

=== QT028 | an assignment where a comparison was meant
r:select from t where a:1

=== clean | times, timestamps and timespans carry colons of their own
r1:select from t where time>09:35
r2:select from t where time=2026.01.01D00:00:00.000
r3:select from t where horizon=0D00:02:00

=== clean | a name ending in where is not the keyword
registry.util.delete.where:{[a] a}

=== QT029 | hopen on a float
h:hopen 1.5

=== QT029 | or a symbol without the colon a handle starts with
h:hopen `abc

=== clean | a port, a handle symbol, and anything only the network can refuse
h1:hopen 5000
h2:hopen `:localhost:5000

=== QT030 | a cast to a character that is no type
r:"Q"$"1"

=== clean | a lowercase type is refused only for some arguments, so it is left alone
c:([]sym:"s"$())

=== QA010 | a unary builtin given two arguments
r:string[1;2]

=== clean | deltas and prev take a second argument
r:deltas[1;1 2 3]


=== QE008 profile: general | monadic minus on a name (q 5: parse "-x" is '-)
f:{-x}

=== QE008 profile: general | after an assignment or another glyph
a:-x
b:1*-x

=== QE008 profile: general | enlist, count and not are keywords in q 5 (',x is ',)
e:,x
g:#x
h:{[y] ~y}

=== clean profile: general | a negative literal, a glyph in parentheses, an amend
a:-1
b:-.5
c:(#)x
d:x-:1

=== clean profile: general | after an operand the glyph is dyadic, even spaced as if it were not
b:x -x
r:x,-1
m:"j"$x
p:`$"a"

=== clean profile: general | an indented line continues the one above
t:a
  ,b

=== clean profile: general | functional forms and iterators
g:@[f;x;0]
h:$[1b;2;3]
e:,/[x]

=== clean profile: general | the sort in select[>a] is qSQL (q 5: select[>a] from ([]a:1 2) sorts)
r:select[>a] from t
s:select[2;<a] from t
u:75_select[>a] from t

=== QE009 profile: general | a derived function applied by juxtaposition (q 5: {+/x} is '/)
f:{+/x}
g:{,/x}

=== QE009 profile: general | a name, a lambda or a noun before the iterator too (q 5: '/ and ')
h:{x/y}
k:{a:count'x}
m:{{x+y}/x}
n:{sum/:x}

=== clean profile: general | in parentheses, with brackets, or infix (q 5 accepts each)
f:{(,/)x}
g:{,/[x]}
h:{x,/:y}
n:{0+/x}
p:{x+/y}
u:{x ~/: y}

=== clean profile: general | a symbol on the left is an operand, and a path is a symbol
y:{` sv'x,'k}
s:{hsym `:hdb/2024}

=== QT025 | a signal at the start of any line, not only the first (q 5: 'stype)
a:1
'1

=== QT025 | or on a lambda's continued line, after its signature
f:{[x]
  '1}

=== clean | a continued line after an operand makes it each
h:{a
  '1}

=== QE007 profile: general | delete needs a from too (q 5: parse "delete a" is 'from)
r:{delete a}

=== QE007 profile: general | and something after it (q 5: parse "select a from" is 'from)
r:{select a from}
s:{delete from}

=== clean profile: general | delete from a named table, and delete columns
delete from t
r:delete a from t
